  "implementation": "ordinaryHitReactions consumes only the required raw CRT draw prefix. It reuses damageKnockdown, mastery thresholds and unarmedBlockRecoil, and returns independent damage-flag/speech/Stagger/suppression/blocked-dispatch/Recoil decisions. The settings adapter resolves typed winning GMST records; compiled defaults remain explicit. No runtime authority/schema/contact admission change.",
  "findings": [
    "Original integer Fatigue<=0 bypasses the damage roll only when scaled incoming Fatigue is positive. A selected pre-scaling damage path can have both final resource arguments zero and still run the stochastic roll.",
    "Positive-Speed Expert/Master ordinary attacks consume a mastery draw even without directional procs.",
    "The speech ratio uses post-contact current integer Health through virtual284, not base Health. At threshold equality it takes a speech draw. That draw uses raw/32767 <= chance; percentile draws use raw%100.",
    "The damage flag requests Stagger only for standing defender/facing attacker. That sets byte4F suppression, skipping later visual398 and force. Lower Block Recoil comes afterward and can coexist on the attacker.",
    "Compiled speech chance .35 differs from installed Oblivion.esm00088FFE .2; installed threshold00088FFF is .1. Raw6553 succeeds and6554 fails at installed chance; raw8000 distinguishes installed from compiled.",
    "The common stage precedes both blocked and lower-skill routing. Current runtime omits this common stage; previous bounded advanced-block/Counter/disarm courses do not establish full-caller RNG parity. Integrate the common stage ahead of both paths and revalidate those courses."
  ],
  "preregistration_errata": [
    "Earlier initial prose baseHealth100 names a supplied virtual284 current integer Health100. Post-health preregistration corrects that identity before edge-case reruns.",
    "The harness field killed supplies the common resource sink boolean. Separate instruction inspection verifies that both sink exits return virtual198; the numeric mVictimRemainsAlive input means its inverse. Runtime must resolve the exact native predicate, not substitute a broader lifecycle convenience gate."
  ],
  "retained_failures": "Attempts01-03 are retained fixture failures: missing actor base/wrong FatigueRatio return cleanup, then omitted positive base-Speed followup on true resource-sink return. Attempt04 and later compositions pass. Component checks01/02 passed their earlier sources; final03 includes denominator/entry corrections and current tests. No failed attempt is promoted to acceptance.",
  "validation_layers": {
    "structural": "New explicit numeric DTO/result and typed GMST adapter compile; no runtime wire/schema changes.",
    "compiler_world": "3001 full normal component tests and854 instrumented ESM4 tests pass with exact inventory and no skips/failures. Engine application/World integration not changed or rebuilt in this chunk.",
    "semantic": "4808 independently executed original caller cases agree with final normal and ASan/UBSan production-object comparisons. Wrong expected Stagger, missing row and invalid raw controls fail as required. Four unit regressions cover order, speech/raw thresholds and winning override, invalid inputs/draws, post-Health/zero-argument entry identity.",
    "runtime": "No new original-game or OpenMW normal-input/render/PCM/restart acceptance. Existing runtime admission remains restricted pending complete consequence publication."
  },
  "integration_requirements": [
    "Use staged post-resource integer Health/Fatigue/Agility/Luck and post-FatigueRatio. Preserve pre-difficulty Health argument separately from the actual difficulty-scaled resource delta.",
    "Preserve the pre-scaling damage-path decision. Do not infer it from final Health/Fatigue deltas.",
    "Keep attack skill and original block/gear/facing context at their verified acquisition points, including incoming weapon breakage; do not re-query changed equipment/posture after Stagger.",
    "Join common reaction/RNG preparation before blocked Counter/BlockHit routing and lower Recoil. Preserve independently resident native slot0 Stagger and slot3 sequences when later dispatch changes process authority.",
    "Prepare speech/voice/combat notification, resource selection RNG and lifetime bindings within the complete contact transaction before removing rejection. No separate live RNG mutation or callback during speculative preparation.",
    "Complete normal-input and real-output fresh-process courses with the full-caller expected RNG and all remaining M15S4 gates."
  ]
